## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Gemini Free Tier Limits**: The implementation caps context at `MAX_CONTEXT_MESSAGES = 10` (last 10 messages) plus recipe metadata and image. This keeps each API call within ~2K tokens of history. Is this limit acceptable, or would you prefer a different cap?

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **TTS Approach**: The plan uses **browser-native SpeechSynthesis API** for text-to-speech (zero server cost, works offline). Browser support for Indian languages (Malayalam, Tamil, Telugu, Kannada) varies by device. If browser TTS quality is insufficient, we can add a gTTS server-side fallback later. Acceptable?

> [!WARNING]
> **Database Migration**: Adding `ChatMessage` requires a DB migration. Since we're using SQLite with `db.create_all()`, the new table will be auto-created. No data loss risk — existing tables are untouched.

## Open Questions

> [!NOTE]
> **Guest Chat History**: The spec says "Guests can use session-only memory." Currently guests can generate recipes but can't save them. Should guest chat messages persist in the Flask session (lost on browser close) or should we skip chat persistence for guests entirely and just keep in-memory during the page session?

> [!NOTE]
> **Image Sending to Gemini**: Sending the uploaded image with every chat message increases Gemini API cost significantly. The plan sends the image only on the **first message** of each chat session and for image-specific questions. Is that acceptable, or should every message include the image?

